{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"P42081","uniProtkbId":"CD86_HUMAN","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"value":"T-lymphocyte activation antigen CD86"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"value":"Activation B7-2 antigen"}},{"fullName":{"value":"B70"}},{"fullName":{"value":"BU63"}},{"fullName":{"value":"CTLA-4 counter-receptor B7.2"}},{"fullName":{"value":"FUN-1"}}],"cdAntigenNames":[{"value":"CD86"}],"flag":"Precursor"},"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P42082"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11279501"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"12196291"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7527824"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7694363"}],"value":"Costimulatory molecule that belongs to the immunoglobulin superfamily that plays an important role in T-lymphocyte activation (PubMed:12196291, PubMed:7694363). Acts as the primary auxiliary signal augmenting the MHC/TCR signal in naive T-cells by acting as a ligand for the CD28 receptor which is constitutively expressed on the cell surface of T-cells (PubMed:12196291, PubMed:7694363). May play a critical role in the early events of T-cell activation and costimulation of naive T-cells, such as deciding between immunity and anergy that is made by T-cells within 24 hours after activation (PubMed:7527824). Also involved in the regulation of B cells function, plays a role in regulating the level of IgG(1) produced. Upon CD40 engagement, activates NF-kappa-B signaling pathway via phospholipase C and protein kinase C activation (By similarity). Also acts as an inhibitor of T-cell activation by acting as a ligand for CTLA4, a decoy receptor, thereby blocking CD28-mediated T-cell priming (PubMed:11279501)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7527824"}],"value":"Interferes with the formation of CD86 clusters, and thus acts as a negative regulator of T-cell activation"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION","molecule":"Isoform 2"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"16920215"}],"value":"(Microbial infection) Acts as a receptor for adenovirus subgroup B"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"7694363"}],"value":"Cell membrane","id":"SL-0039"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"11279501"}],"value":"Single-pass type I membrane protein","id":"SL-9905"}}]}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":23,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":248,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":268,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Helical","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":33,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":131,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Ig-like V-type"},{"type":"Domain","location":{"start":{"value":150,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":225,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Ig-like C2-type"},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":277,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":329,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Disordered","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Compositional bias","location":{"start":{"value":287,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":312,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Basic and acidic residues","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000256","source":"SAM","id":"MobiDB-lite"}]},{"type":"Glycosylation","location":{"start":{"value":33,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":33,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"N-linked (GlcNAc...) asparagine","evidences":[{"evidence